            <ArticleTitle>[Treatment of chronic pain in advanced malignant disease by oral morphine (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>3119-21</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Fifty one patients with terminal cancer suffering severe pains reluctant to other treatment have received morphine by mouth, in a regular regimen. The doses range between 5 and 50 mg every 4 hours. 60% of our patients have their pain alleviated without any side effect impeding the treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
